1
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,125
Now I get it.

2
00:00:15,166 --> 00:00:18,125
This is that big-mouthed
monster's natural habitat.

3
00:00:18,125 --> 00:00:20,125
The death knell it let out was a lure

4
00:00:20,166 --> 00:00:23,000
to draw a huge horde here.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,125
The pandemonium is enough to terrify
even what lives in this monstrous land.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,041
Sir Tooka...

7
00:00:31,125 --> 00:00:33,125
We still have some time before they arrive.

8
00:00:34,041 --> 00:00:36,125
There's... There's an
outrageous number of them.

9
00:00:36,125 --> 00:00:38,083
Knowing that is enough.

10
00:00:39,125 --> 00:00:41,041
Everyone, listen to me.

11
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:45,000
I'll act as bait and draw the monsters to me.

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,083
Use the time I buy to get to the witch.

13
00:00:48,166 --> 00:00:51,208
I'll create an opportunity for you all
to escape, no matter what.

14
00:00:51,208 --> 00:00:52,208
Big Sis!

15
00:00:52,208 --> 00:00:53,208
Lis.

16
00:00:54,041 --> 00:00:56,208
My own carelessness brought this on us.

17
00:00:56,208 --> 00:00:59,000
I must be the one to take action.

18
00:00:59,125 --> 00:01:02,208
As you know, my senses are quite sharp.

19
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,208
I'm also an expert at maneuvering
in terrain like this.

20
00:01:07,041 --> 00:01:08,083
Big Sis...

21
00:01:08,125 --> 00:01:12,166
Lis, make sure you listen
to Tooka and Seras until I return.

22
00:01:12,166 --> 00:01:13,208
- Lis, make sure you listen
to Tooka and Seras until I return.
- All right.

23
00:01:15,041 --> 00:01:19,083
If you're that insistent,
I'll let you lure them away.

24
00:01:19,208 --> 00:01:22,083
But on one condition.

25
00:01:22,083 --> 00:01:24,000
You have to promise us

26
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:26,083
that you'll make it back alive.

27
00:01:26,166 --> 00:01:29,208
- Yes, you have my word.
- Did you think I'd agree just like that?

28
00:01:31,083 --> 00:01:32,208
Tooka?

29
00:01:37,125 --> 00:01:41,166
TO THE LIMIT, AND BEYOND
- Eve, your odds of survival are too low.

30
00:01:41,208 --> 00:01:43,041
But I...

31
00:01:44,208 --> 00:01:47,208
First of all, you don't
need to feel responsible.

32
00:01:48,208 --> 00:01:50,166
The monster you cut down

33
00:01:50,166 --> 00:01:54,041
kept hidden until it was
within extremely close range,

34
00:01:54,083 --> 00:01:56,041
then broke concealment without warning.

35
00:01:56,125 --> 00:01:59,083
It would have been a challenge
for you to sense it ahead of time.

36
00:01:59,125 --> 00:02:00,083
Still!

37
00:02:00,125 --> 00:02:03,000
Had I been the one standing where you were,

38
00:02:03,041 --> 00:02:05,041
I would have done the same thing.

39
00:02:05,041 --> 00:02:08,000
I should've used my status
ailment skill immediately.

40
00:02:08,083 --> 00:02:10,166
So this is on me, too.

41
00:02:11,041 --> 00:02:13,083
No reason for you to take all the blame.

42
00:02:13,125 --> 00:02:14,125
But Tooka—

43
00:02:14,125 --> 00:02:15,083
Listen.

44
00:02:15,125 --> 00:02:19,000
Eve Speed, you're indispensable
in getting us to the witch.

45
00:02:19,041 --> 00:02:22,083
She bestowed your kind with that map.

46
00:02:22,208 --> 00:02:25,041
Bringing someone she's entrusted it to

47
00:02:25,041 --> 00:02:26,208
will make our negotiations much easier.

48
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,083
My voice projection gem...

49
00:02:29,125 --> 00:02:32,125
It isn't fully hardened yet,
but it is solid now.

50
00:02:32,208 --> 00:02:34,208
I just hope it functions.

51
00:02:35,125 --> 00:02:40,000
I'm the one with the best chance
at survival given the situation.

52
00:02:40,125 --> 00:02:43,208
Or, to be more accurate,
me, Piggymaru, and Slei.

53
00:02:44,083 --> 00:02:47,041
This team has the best shot at ensuring
we all make it out alive.

54
00:02:49,083 --> 00:02:50,125
Besides, at present,

55
00:02:50,166 --> 00:02:54,041
my status ailment skill is the only thing
guaranteed to deliver lethal damage

56
00:02:54,041 --> 00:02:56,041
to the human-faced beasts.

57
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,208
Responsibility is important,

58
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,083
but I decide where that responsibility
falls within our war band.

59
00:03:02,166 --> 00:03:05,125
So if I say not to worry about it, then don't.

60
00:03:05,125 --> 00:03:07,041
That's an order.

61
00:03:07,125 --> 00:03:09,000
Forgive me.

62
00:03:09,208 --> 00:03:13,041
I can't say I don't like
your strong sense of duty.

63
00:03:13,083 --> 00:03:15,125
Sir Tooka, thank you so much.

64
00:03:15,125 --> 00:03:17,041
It's still too early for thanks.

65
00:03:17,208 --> 00:03:21,041
Save it for after we've all
reached our destination safely.

66
00:03:21,125 --> 00:03:22,125
Yes!

67
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,083
Sir Tooka...

68
00:03:36,083 --> 00:03:37,166
Good luck.

69
00:03:38,125 --> 00:03:41,125
If I don't return, I leave
the rest in your hands.

70
00:03:41,166 --> 00:03:42,125
Yes!

71
00:03:42,166 --> 00:03:47,125
I'd like to ask you not
to say such ominous things,

72
00:03:47,125 --> 00:03:49,166
but for now, I shall simply accept it.

73
00:03:49,166 --> 00:03:52,041
I'm glad you're an
understanding vice captain.

74
00:03:56,208 --> 00:03:58,083
Everyone, run!

75
00:03:58,166 --> 00:04:00,000
Don't get caught in it!

76
00:04:02,041 --> 00:04:04,083
Everyone, hurry up and move!

77
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,125
Suou-san, please lead them!

78
00:04:06,166 --> 00:04:08,000
Okay, got it!

79
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,166
Everyone! This way!

80
00:04:13,041 --> 00:04:15,208
Kanae-san! Everyone, wait!

81
00:04:17,125 --> 00:04:19,166
What's all the uproar about?

82
00:04:19,166 --> 00:04:22,041
What is wrong with these things?!

83
00:04:28,083 --> 00:04:29,166
We're nothing...

84
00:04:32,083 --> 00:04:34,125
but an obstacle to them?

85
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,208
I don't want to die! I don't want to die!

86
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,083
Kanae-san!

87
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Thanks, little pigeon!

88
00:04:54,041 --> 00:04:57,125
It's all right... No one's died yet...

89
00:04:57,166 --> 00:04:58,208
Not a single person...

90
00:05:03,125 --> 00:05:05,041
That's not true.

91
00:05:08,166 --> 00:05:10,000
They're close.

92
00:05:10,041 --> 00:05:11,083
It's almost time, huh?

93
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,041
I ordered Seras and the others to hide
in a cave we found along the way.

94
00:05:18,125 --> 00:05:19,166
That just leaves...

95
00:05:37,041 --> 00:05:38,083
Here we go!

96
00:05:50,166 --> 00:05:52,041
This spot should be good.

97
00:05:56,041 --> 00:05:59,166
You'll be the one to signal the
start of battle, Piggymaru.

98
00:06:00,166 --> 00:06:01,166
Go for it.

99
00:06:23,041 --> 00:06:25,166
Glad you've all got such good hearing.

100
00:06:25,166 --> 00:06:28,125
Taking the bait like damned honest fools...

101
00:06:29,166 --> 00:06:33,083
From here on, it's going
to be a high-speed chase.

102
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,041
No telling if I'll survive this.

103
00:06:45,166 --> 00:06:48,000
Depending on the strength
of those human-faced beasts,

104
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,041
I could be done for.

105
00:06:49,125 --> 00:06:52,166
Still, I can't afford to let my worry show.

106
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,125
Sorry, you two.

107
00:06:56,166 --> 00:06:59,125
Will you put your lives in my hands?

108
00:07:03,083 --> 00:07:05,041
Yeah, you're right.

109
00:07:05,041 --> 00:07:06,083
Let me rephrase.

110
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Will you put your lives
in my hands for their sake?

111
00:07:17,125 --> 00:07:19,041
Assault Accel!

112
00:07:25,083 --> 00:07:26,125
Now...

113
00:07:37,041 --> 00:07:39,125
Let's wage this all-out war!

114
00:07:45,166 --> 00:07:46,166
It can't be...

115
00:07:54,041 --> 00:07:55,041
Yasu-kun.

116
00:07:55,041 --> 00:07:57,041
Oh, it's you, Ayaka?

117
00:07:57,208 --> 00:07:59,125
Hirooka-kun and Sakuma-kun

118
00:07:59,125 --> 00:08:01,125
were part of your group, right?

119
00:08:01,125 --> 00:08:03,041
- Weren't you with them?
- We should be prioritizing the safety
of higher-ranking heroes like me.

120
00:08:03,083 --> 00:08:06,208
We should be prioritizing the safety
of higher-ranking heroes like me.

121
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:11,166
We can't afford to have our best talent
taking unnecessary damage here.

122
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,125
So it goes without saying that this was
their fault for being slow to flee.

123
00:08:16,125 --> 00:08:19,041
I-It goes without saying...?

124
00:08:19,083 --> 00:08:23,041
You didn't do anything when the
stampede of monsters appeared?!

125
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,041
What are you trying to say, Ayaka?

126
00:08:26,083 --> 00:08:28,041
Y-You're A-Class!

127
00:08:28,041 --> 00:08:29,041
Yes, and?

128
00:08:29,041 --> 00:08:32,166
Don't you feel a duty to protect
the classmates in your group?!

129
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,125
The students under you are relying on you.

130
00:08:37,125 --> 00:08:40,083
So you need to protect them!

131
00:08:40,083 --> 00:08:42,166
Yasu-kun, you were the only one
there who could have...

132
00:08:42,208 --> 00:08:44,166
Sh-Sh-Sh...

133
00:08:44,208 --> 00:08:46,041
Shut up!

134
00:08:46,083 --> 00:08:48,083
Shut up, shut up, shut up!

135
00:08:48,083 --> 00:08:51,208
Shut your mouth, Ayaka!

136
00:08:52,083 --> 00:08:53,041
Huh?

137
00:08:53,083 --> 00:08:54,125
Wh-What is your problem?!

138
00:08:54,166 --> 00:08:57,125
Why are you still acting like
you're so much better than me?!

139
00:08:57,166 --> 00:08:58,208
Why're you so condescending?!

140
00:08:58,208 --> 00:09:00,083
Where's your sense of hierarchy?!

141
00:09:00,125 --> 00:09:01,125
Face facts already!

142
00:09:01,166 --> 00:09:02,208
Wh-What are you talking about?

143
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,208
There, there, there! That's it, yes!

144
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,166
That's how you always are, Sogou Ayaka!

145
00:09:06,166 --> 00:09:10,041
You aren't even consciously
aware of it most of the time!

146
00:09:10,083 --> 00:09:12,125
You just naturally look down on others!

147
00:09:12,125 --> 00:09:13,125
Hold on!

148
00:09:13,125 --> 00:09:17,000
I was saying you should have protected them—

149
00:09:17,041 --> 00:09:18,125
Not my problem!

150
00:09:18,166 --> 00:09:20,125
I survived because I was strong!

151
00:09:20,166 --> 00:09:22,083
They died because they were weak!

152
00:09:22,083 --> 00:09:24,000
It's as simple as that!

153
00:09:24,041 --> 00:09:26,125
The strong have a responsibility
to shield those without—

154
00:09:26,125 --> 00:09:27,208
There, see?!

155
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,208
Ayaka, you so naturally speak
like you're one of the strong!

156
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,125
That's what I'm talking about!

157
00:09:33,125 --> 00:09:34,208
This noblesse oblige crap!

158
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,083
You always act like a saint
while looking down on others!

159
00:09:37,125 --> 00:09:40,166
Constantly flaunting the difference
between us without intending to be mean!

160
00:09:40,166 --> 00:09:44,083
For starters, both Hirooka and
Sakuma deserved to die anyway!

161
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:46,125
When shitty, weak, little
Mimori got sent to hell,

162
00:09:46,125 --> 00:09:49,083
they were the first to dog on him!

163
00:09:49,083 --> 00:09:52,166
They constantly made fun
of me behind my back too!

164
00:09:52,166 --> 00:09:54,041
You reap what you sow!

165
00:09:54,083 --> 00:09:55,083
Or what?

166
00:09:55,083 --> 00:09:58,041
Does Miss Class President
who's been blessed from birth

167
00:09:58,083 --> 00:09:59,208
think I should feel sorry for them too?!

168
00:09:59,208 --> 00:10:01,041
You're such a nobody.

169
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,083
Kirihara!

170
00:10:03,083 --> 00:10:06,208
Yasu, do you know what they say
about the measure of a man?

171
00:10:08,125 --> 00:10:12,125
Everyone has an inborn caliber,

172
00:10:12,125 --> 00:10:16,125
and it's only after you make it
that people know if you truly measure up.

173
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:21,083
If you don't, then your success
will only be temporary.

174
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,083
Are you following me?

175
00:10:24,125 --> 00:10:27,083
What are you trying to say?

176
00:10:27,166 --> 00:10:30,041
You even react like a nobody, Yasu.

177
00:10:30,083 --> 00:10:31,125
Take a hint.

178
00:10:31,166 --> 00:10:36,000
What could I possibly mean other than
that you're drastically beneath me?

179
00:10:38,041 --> 00:10:40,041
You proved you were a nobody

180
00:10:40,041 --> 00:10:45,083
when you forgot your flimsy act
and lost it in front of Sogou.

181
00:10:45,083 --> 00:10:48,000
There's no excuse for a nobody like you.

182
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:52,125
Holding power beyond your lowly station

183
00:10:52,125 --> 00:10:55,083
will have you disgracing
yourself before you know it.

184
00:10:55,125 --> 00:10:59,166
Tremendous power should be wielded by none
other than those with royal caliber, like me.

185
00:10:59,208 --> 00:11:02,208
Though I pity you a little
for getting the wrong idea

186
00:11:02,208 --> 00:11:04,208
after being deemed A-Class.

187
00:11:04,208 --> 00:11:06,125
Screw you, Kirihara!

188
00:11:06,166 --> 00:11:08,125
Laevateinn!

189
00:11:09,083 --> 00:11:10,083
Yasu-kun!

190
00:11:10,125 --> 00:11:11,083
Huh?

191
00:11:11,125 --> 00:11:14,000
Why're you blowing your lid
and snapping on us?

192
00:11:14,083 --> 00:11:18,125
So you're truly an irredeemable
nobody, Yasu Tomohiro?

193
00:11:19,125 --> 00:11:22,000
Don't get it twisted
just because you're S-Class.

194
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,125
You're the one who needs
to take a hint, Kirihara Takuto!

195
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,208
There's still a hero who hasn't learned
a unique skill despite being S-Class,

196
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:34,083
even when all the other S-Class
heroes have theirs already.

197
00:11:34,166 --> 00:11:37,208
See? Ayaka herself is proof.

198
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
And then there's Asagi,
who's learned a unique skill

199
00:11:41,041 --> 00:11:41,208
- that surpasses Oyamada's at A-Class,
despite the fact that she's B-Class!
- Huh?!

200
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,041
that surpasses Oyamada's at A-Class,
despite the fact that she's B-Class!

201
00:11:45,125 --> 00:11:48,208
You understand what I'm
trying to say, right?

202
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:53,166
In other words,
our hero rank isn't everything.

203
00:11:53,208 --> 00:11:56,125
So assuming you're above us
just because you're S-Class...

204
00:11:56,125 --> 00:11:59,208
is what a nobody getting
the wrong idea really looks like!

205
00:12:00,083 --> 00:12:02,166
Eventually I'll show you which of us

206
00:12:02,208 --> 00:12:06,125
is truly of royal caliber, you dumb bastard.

207
00:12:06,166 --> 00:12:07,125
Why, you...

208
00:12:07,208 --> 00:12:09,208
Stop it, Shougo.

209
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,041
Why?!

210
00:12:11,041 --> 00:12:13,166
You're not gonna tell me you're
scared of him, are you?

211
00:12:14,041 --> 00:12:15,041
Huh?

212
00:12:15,125 --> 00:12:19,208
Oh, er, um... My bad.

213
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,041
Hmph. You're the nobodies.

214
00:12:24,083 --> 00:12:28,000
I may be forced to admit
there's someone dragging down

215
00:12:28,041 --> 00:12:29,208
the rest of us S-Class heroes.

216
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:33,166
You need to understand the
position you're in already, Sogou.

217
00:12:44,041 --> 00:12:47,083
I guess I need to demonstrate my caliber

218
00:12:47,125 --> 00:12:50,041
so that even you dense fools can grasp it.

219
00:12:52,125 --> 00:12:53,208
I'm...

220
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,125
Asagi, I don't see the little pigeon.

221
00:12:58,125 --> 00:13:00,083
What, really?

222
00:13:01,125 --> 00:13:03,000
Well, she'll find her way back.

223
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:03,208
Yeah.

224
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,083
She's missing? Kashima-san's gone?

225
00:13:09,125 --> 00:13:11,125
I'll go after Tooka.

226
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,083
Please tell me your reasoning.

227
00:13:15,125 --> 00:13:17,125
There were too many monsters.

228
00:13:17,125 --> 00:13:21,041
Even with his stat adjustments,
they're not everything.

229
00:13:21,083 --> 00:13:24,125
More importantly,
Tooka's not in peak condition.

230
00:13:24,208 --> 00:13:26,166
Ever since we hit the Land of Monsters,

231
00:13:26,208 --> 00:13:29,083
he's gotten the least sleep of all of us.

232
00:13:29,125 --> 00:13:33,125
I'm guessing he's been periodically
using "Sleep" on the rest of us,

233
00:13:34,041 --> 00:13:37,166
all so we can slumber soundly
here in the Land of Monsters.

234
00:13:37,208 --> 00:13:41,166
Sir Tooka has been sacrificing
his own rest since entering this land

235
00:13:41,208 --> 00:13:44,041
in order to bolster our hope.

236
00:13:44,041 --> 00:13:48,000
Thanks to that, we've managed
to make it to the heartland.

237
00:13:48,083 --> 00:13:51,208
I wasn't just talking a big game
before we parted ways.

238
00:13:51,208 --> 00:13:55,125
Hiding my presence and maneuvering
in this kind of terrain is my forte.

239
00:13:55,208 --> 00:13:57,125
I also have night vision when it gets dark,

240
00:13:57,166 --> 00:14:00,125
so I don't need to worry about a light
giving my position away.

241
00:14:00,166 --> 00:14:02,000
I have sharp ears as ell.

242
00:14:02,125 --> 00:14:05,208
I can tell those aren't baseless
lies to make me feel better.

243
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:06,208
Moreover...

244
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,125
if Tooka or Slei are badly wounded,

245
00:14:09,125 --> 00:14:11,041
I'm the only one who can carry them.

246
00:14:11,125 --> 00:14:14,083
We cannot afford to lose that man here.

247
00:14:15,166 --> 00:14:19,083
I understand you're not acting
based on rash sentiments.

248
00:14:19,083 --> 00:14:20,125
I thank you.

249
00:14:21,041 --> 00:14:22,166
Forgive me.

250
00:14:23,125 --> 00:14:24,208
With Sir Tooka absent,

251
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:29,041
I believe it's my duty to make decisions
for the safety of our group.

252
00:14:29,208 --> 00:14:32,166
So I'm sorry for testing you like that.

253
00:14:33,125 --> 00:14:36,125
You truly are fond of that man, aren't you?

254
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:37,166
Yes.

255
00:14:37,208 --> 00:14:40,041
I have devoted myself to him, after all.

256
00:14:43,083 --> 00:14:44,125
Big Sis?

257
00:14:46,083 --> 00:14:49,000
Be sure you listen to Seras, okay?

258
00:14:53,041 --> 00:14:56,000
Please take care of Sir Tooka.

259
00:14:57,041 --> 00:14:59,083
I'm sorry, Lis.

260
00:15:00,166 --> 00:15:04,041
Please promise me this.
Promise that you'll return alive.

261
00:15:04,041 --> 00:15:07,208
Of course. I'm entrusting Lis to you, Seras.

262
00:15:07,208 --> 00:15:10,125
I'll do whatever it takes to protect her.

263
00:15:10,166 --> 00:15:13,041
Whatever it takes, huh?

264
00:15:13,166 --> 00:15:16,083
Perhaps that's Tooka's
influence showing as well.

265
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:18,083
Okay, I'm heading out.

266
00:15:23,166 --> 00:15:27,125
Wherever I fire, I'm bound to hit one of them.

267
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,125
So my first move...

268
00:15:29,208 --> 00:15:31,000
is to spread out.

269
00:15:33,083 --> 00:15:34,083
Do it!

270
00:15:41,166 --> 00:15:42,166
Berserk!

271
00:16:00,041 --> 00:16:02,083
That only scrambled them for a moment?

272
00:16:02,166 --> 00:16:04,208
They switch gears too damn fast.

273
00:16:05,083 --> 00:16:07,125
Choosing to kill over being killed...

274
00:16:07,166 --> 00:16:09,166
Choosing to fight for survival...

275
00:16:13,166 --> 00:16:14,208
Paralyze!

276
00:16:24,208 --> 00:16:28,125
My surprise attack only stalled them
for a few seconds, buying me no time.

277
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,125
Also, the human-faced beasts in the front
that are adapting to my tentacle attacks

278
00:16:33,166 --> 00:16:35,000
are still alive and well.

279
00:16:38,041 --> 00:16:41,041
The stampede of monsters
lured you in too, huh?

280
00:16:41,208 --> 00:16:43,041
Piggymaru, Slei!

281
00:16:43,083 --> 00:16:44,125
Can you still keep going?

282
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,208
The rain's dampening sounds.

283
00:16:56,125 --> 00:16:58,208
I can't follow them with just my ears now.

284
00:16:59,083 --> 00:17:01,125
Can't say visibility's good either.

285
00:17:01,125 --> 00:17:03,000
Status: Open.

286
00:17:03,041 --> 00:17:07,000
TOOKA MIMORI
- Combining with Piggymaru
is essential to this battle.

287
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,125
However, at the rate things are going,

288
00:17:08,166 --> 00:17:10,208
I can only keep this up ten more minutes.

289
00:17:11,083 --> 00:17:13,083
To stay in the game, I'll have to level up.

290
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,125
The human-faced beasts are
worth a ton of EXP.

291
00:17:16,125 --> 00:17:19,208
As long as I can keep killing them
and keep leveling up...

292
00:17:24,208 --> 00:17:27,125
No, that's definitely too reckless.

293
00:17:27,125 --> 00:17:31,166
Plus, if I'm not within a certain range,
then I don't get any EXP when they die.

294
00:17:31,208 --> 00:17:35,125
That means I'll have to double back
the way we came.

295
00:17:36,041 --> 00:17:39,208
If I say I've got this,
will you two follow me?

296
00:17:42,208 --> 00:17:44,000
Truly...

297
00:17:46,125 --> 00:17:48,208
I am truly blessed with allies.

298
00:17:55,083 --> 00:17:56,083
Here we go!

299
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:05,041
Dark!

300
00:18:10,125 --> 00:18:12,208
TOOKA MIMORI

301
00:18:13,041 --> 00:18:14,208
Dark! Dark!

302
00:18:14,208 --> 00:18:16,041
Paralyze! Paralyze!

303
00:18:16,083 --> 00:18:17,125
Berserk!

304
00:18:28,041 --> 00:18:29,041
Slei!

305
00:18:29,208 --> 00:18:32,125
TOOKA MIMORI

306
00:18:33,125 --> 00:18:34,166
We're there.

307
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,125
Welcome...

308
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,125
TOOKA MIMORI

309
00:18:39,166 --> 00:18:41,000
into my range!

310
00:18:44,041 --> 00:18:45,125
TOOKA MIMORI

311
00:18:45,166 --> 00:18:47,000
Berserk!

312
00:18:52,041 --> 00:18:53,125
Now...

313
00:18:58,083 --> 00:18:59,208
You have leveled up.

314
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,208
TOOKA MIMORI
- My MP's fully restored!

315
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,208
I can maintain combat!

316
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Piggymaru!

317
00:19:06,166 --> 00:19:11,208
I need to keep track of how far I can
earn EXP in this quasi-localized war.

318
00:19:11,208 --> 00:19:15,125
It's the only way for us to fight and survive.

319
00:19:15,166 --> 00:19:17,125
Paralyze! Berserk!

320
00:19:20,125 --> 00:19:22,041
I have plenty of MP.

321
00:19:22,166 --> 00:19:25,125
Now we just try to kill each other.

322
00:19:27,125 --> 00:19:31,000
Two huge-ass monsters are on my tail.

323
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:35,208
Sleep!

324
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,083
My status ailment skill

325
00:19:37,125 --> 00:19:41,000
requires me to have them in my line
of sight in order to affect them.

326
00:19:54,041 --> 00:19:55,083
Behind you.

327
00:19:57,083 --> 00:19:58,083
Paralyze!

328
00:20:02,125 --> 00:20:04,166
Berserk! Berserk!

329
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:11,166
You have leveled up.

330
00:20:11,166 --> 00:20:13,000
TOOKA MIMORI

331
00:20:27,208 --> 00:20:30,000
Paralyze! Berserk!

332
00:20:30,166 --> 00:20:33,041
Dark! Paralyze!

333
00:20:35,208 --> 00:20:36,166
Par—!

334
00:20:36,166 --> 00:20:37,166
Dark!

335
00:20:49,208 --> 00:20:50,208
Paralyze!

336
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,000
Berserk!

337
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:52,208
Sleep!

338
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,166
Dark!

339
00:20:54,208 --> 00:20:55,166
Berserk!

340
00:20:55,208 --> 00:20:57,000
Paralyze!

341
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:57,208
Dark!

342
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,083
Paralyze!

343
00:20:59,166 --> 00:21:01,041
Sir Tooka!

344
00:21:01,125 --> 00:21:02,208
You have leveled up.

345
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,166
You have leveled up.

346
00:21:04,208 --> 00:21:06,125
You have leveled up.

347
00:21:06,166 --> 00:21:09,125
- You have leveled up.
You have leveled up.
- Kill and slaughter, kill and slaughter...

348
00:21:09,166 --> 00:21:12,000
Kill and slaughter, kill and slaughter...

349
00:21:16,083 --> 00:21:17,083
I can't...

350
00:21:18,041 --> 00:21:19,166
I know.

351
00:21:19,166 --> 00:21:22,083
I'm not like Sogou-san.

352
00:21:22,083 --> 00:21:26,208
All I could do was hide and watch when
they did that to Mimori-kun too.

353
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:29,166
Even so, I wanted to be useful.

354
00:21:29,208 --> 00:21:33,041
I wanted to be able to care for others
even in awful moments like Sogou-san...

355
00:21:33,041 --> 00:21:34,166
But I'm scared!

356
00:21:34,208 --> 00:21:36,000
I'm going to die!

357
00:21:41,041 --> 00:21:44,125
What's a human doing in a place like this?

358
00:21:51,083 --> 00:21:52,125
They're similar.

359
00:21:55,083 --> 00:21:57,000
THE ONE WHO CIRCULATES LIGHTNING
- Lightning Shifter, Unlock One.

360
00:21:57,041 --> 00:21:58,000
THE ONE WHO CIRCULATES LIGHTNING
UNLOCK STAGE ONE
- Lightning Shifter, Unlock One.

361
00:22:03,083 --> 00:22:04,125
Hey, you—

362
00:22:04,125 --> 00:22:06,041
UNLOCK STAGE TWO
- Unlock Two.

363
00:22:08,041 --> 00:22:11,083
Not only did you react to Stage One,
you withstood the damn blow...

364
00:22:11,125 --> 00:22:14,125
But you can't escape my lightning now.

365
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:17,125
My throat... I can't speak...

366
00:22:17,125 --> 00:22:18,166
Sorry.

367
00:22:18,208 --> 00:22:22,208
On my sister's orders,
I can't let you kill Kashima.

368
00:22:23,083 --> 00:22:24,166
Itsuki-san...

369
00:22:25,083 --> 00:22:27,125
I see. These girls are...

370
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,125
Tooka told me about them.

371
00:22:29,125 --> 00:22:33,166
They're the ones summoned by the goddess
to defeat the source of evil...

372
00:22:33,166 --> 00:22:35,041
The heroes from another world!

373
00:24:10,166 --> 00:24:14,208
RULER AND SWORD

